{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂er-|*deḱ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|Art déco|Art Déco}}, first used in the catalogue of an exhibition at the Musée des Arts Decoratifs in Paris, France, in 1966. {{m|fr||Art Déco}} is a {{clipping|fr|[[arts]] [[décoratifs]]|t=decorative arts|nocap=1}} (from the name of an exhibition called ''L’Exposition Internationale des Arts Décoratifs et Industriels Modernes'' (The International Exhibition of Modern Decorative and Industrial Arts) held in Paris in 1925), from {{m|fr|arts}} ({{glossary|plural}} of {{m|fr|art|t=art}}) + {{m|fr|décoratifs}} (plural of {{m|fr|décoratif|t=decorative}}).<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=5569037187|date=September 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|entry=art deco|pos=n}}</ref>

