===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|architecture|art}} A [[style#Noun|style]] of [[decorative#Adjective|decorative]] [[art#Noun|art]] (often [[use#Verb|used]] in [[household#Noun|household]] [[object#Noun|objects]]) and [[architecture]] [[originate|originating]] in the 1920s and 1930s, [[characterize]]d by [[bold#Adjective|bold]] [[geometric]] [[form#Noun|forms]], [[strong#Adjective|strong]] [[contrasting#Adjective|contrasting]] [[color#Noun|colours]], and [[simple#Adjective|simple]] [[composition]]. {{defdate|from 1966}}
#: {{synonyms|en|Deco}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 December 15|author=Robin Leleux|title=Awards honour the best restoration projects: The Great Western Railway Craft Skills Award: Victoria Arcade|journal=RAIL|issue=946|page=59|text=This project has stripped away modern PVCu and aluminium shop fronts to reveal original or 1930s '''Art Deco''' work, with judicious repairs and replacements as necessary, plus stonework repairs and the restoration of traditional London Transport signage.}}

